  "body": "What happens: the maintainer ran the test build of PR #2243 (`camcraft-2235-367f48185.exe`, v0.22.0 · 9695ea08) on `testdata/models/fig8.camproj`. Edge selection is fast now. But when the operation shows its filled area preview (the orange band outside the part, 2D Adaptive, Containment `Outside`, a welded face of 424 strips selected), the frame rate drops.\n\nThe words of the maintainer, 2026-11-16: \"2235, selecting eddges performs well.. that \"visualized\" outside area in orange tho.. It dropped framerate\"\n\nEvidence (his log):\n\n```\nWARN generate{op=2D Adaptive1}: camcraft_app::operation::generate::run_job: generation refused: invalid machining parameters: adaptive: the center area has no room for an entry kind=2D Adaptive ms=72\ngpu: slow frame 201 ms (budget 100 ms, 1 slow so far) - slowest phase \"commands\" 94 ms [commands 94 ms, scene 22 ms, ui 84 ms, acquire 0 ms, encode 0 ms, submit+present 0 ms]\n```\n\nThe slow phases are `commands` (94 ms) and `ui` (84 ms), not `scene`. The log has one slow frame at the moment of the refused generate. The maintainer reports a lower frame rate while the band shows. The cause is not known: find it with a measurement before a fix.\n\nExpected: a frame with the area preview on screen stays under 10 ms when nothing changed (target of #2235 and #2238). The area fill is derived data: compute it one time for each change of its inputs and cache the mesh.\n\nRelated: #2235 / PR #2243 (selected-chain frame cost; this work stacks on that branch), #2201 (hover path, a different claim), #2232 (the refusal \"no room for an entry\" itself), #2238 (cache strategy).\n\nNot in scope: the refusal text and the entry strategy (#2232). The area that the preview shows and the cut geometry must not change.\n\nDone means: a test pins that a frame without a change builds no area fill and runs no generate-side work; the measured cost of the `commands` and `ui` phases with the preview shown is in the PR; the maintainer has a test build.\n",
